# card-sheet-tool (read-only reference)

`card-sheet-tool` is **not** part of this repo. It is in the workspace for reference only
(it lives at `~/Downloads/projects/battle/card-sheet-tool`).

- **Never modify** any file under `card-sheet-tool/`. Do not refactor, fix or "clean up" it unless the user explicitly revokes this rule.
- Implement new code **only under `void-matter-online`**. Copy and adapt logic; never edit the reference tree.

## It is not the rulebook

It is the old **simulator**, and it differs from the V5 rulebook and from the owner's rulings. Where it conflicts with the docs, **the docs win** (see `docs-source-of-truth.mdc`).

- For combat behaviour, read `docs/design-decisions.md` sections 3, 7 and 15 first. Section 15 overrides everything earlier.
- `docs/combat-reference.md` describes the simulator, starts with a list of overrides, and is **stale in many places**. Use it only for numeric tables and component lists, after reading the banner.
- Open `card-sheet-tool` source only for exact component or enemy tables, or for parity checks against the simulator (`playerComponents.ts`, `enemyShips.ts`, `combatEngine.ts` and similar).
- When you copy a number or behaviour from it, check it against `design-decisions.md`, and cite the ruling ID that overrides it if one exists.
